{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/concepts/exceptions","title":"Exceptions as values","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"exceptions-as-values","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Exceptions as values"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A declared failure is a "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"value you return"}]},{"t":"text","text":", not something you throw. It travels"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"through types instead of escaping through the stack — so the compiler can see it,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"follow it, and tell you when nobody handled it."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"That is the whole idea, and it rests on a line most codebases leave blurry:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"an "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"exception"}]},{"t":"text","text":" is a failure you declared, expect, and intend to handle —"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"\"this email is taken\", \"the session expired\", \"that id is malformed\";"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"an "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"error"}]},{"t":"text","text":" is everything else — the unexpected kind, which should surface"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"loudly rather than be silently absorbed."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A "},{"t":"code","text":"try/catch"},{"t":"text","text":" tells you nothing about what it might catch. A returned"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"craftException"},{"t":"text","text":" carries its code and payload all the way to whoever handles it,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"and the set of reachable codes is a "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"type"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — which is what makes exhaustive"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"checking possible at all."}]},{"t":"headin